This page is Sowa's.
.Sh CAVEATS
Landlock covers the filesystem, TCP bind and connect, and a small set of
scopes.
It does not cover UDP, raw sockets, ptrace beyond the scope options, or the
loading of a kernel module, and it is not a substitute for
.Xr seccomp 2
where the concern is which system calls are reachable at all.
.Pp
A ruleset applies to paths, not to files: a hard link created outside a granted
hierarchy is outside it, and a bind mount into one is inside it.
